     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Anthony,<div><br></div><div>Thank you for your interest in TITAN.  TitanCNA requires input data from germline heterozygous SNP sites.  This is generally determined from the matched normal.  In your situation, it appears you do not have the matched normal setup. Can you confirm this?  In the figures, we can see many homozygous SNPs which I suspect are probably not heterozygous in the germline.  </div><div><br></div><div>TitanCNA requires matched tumour-normal pairs, particularly for identifying germline heterozygous SNPs.  There is growing interest for applying TitanCNA to tumour-only samples; however, this is not currently included as a feature.  </div><div><br></div><div>Hope this helps.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Gavin</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
